cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RunFix in academic work, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "RunFix: autonomous diagnosis, safe repair and experiment reproduction for research code"
abstract: >-
  RunFix is an agent for research repositories. It reads a project's README, manifests,
  configuration and entrypoints, diagnoses its environment, builds an evidence graph from a
  failure, ranks root causes with cited evidence, applies patches as reversible transactions,
  and runs the documented experiment behind an evidence ladder that refuses to treat a zero
  exit code as a reproduction. It exposes the same capabilities through a CLI, an MCP server
  and a local web console, with hash-chained auditing of every privileged action.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "RunFix contributors"
